From: Eduardo Fockink <54868856+EduardoFockink@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: mgpu copy module (AQ_MGPU_GPU_COPY, AQ_MGPU_CPU_COPY) for NVIDIA-render / Intel-scanout

For an output on a secondary GPU, the primary copies each frame's damaged region into a linear buffer the
secondary only scans out, instead of the secondary importing the primary's buffer (an NVIDIA primary cannot
render into LINEAR and Mesa cannot read NVIDIA's native layout).

  AQ_MGPU_GPU_COPY  the primary's Vulkan copy engine writes a buffer it exported; KMS waits on the copy's fence
  AQ_MGPU_CPU_COPY  the primary reads the region back into a dumb buffer of the secondary (also the fallback)

Everything lives in src/backend/drm/mgpu. Upstream files only carry hooks (36 lines): DRM.cpp, GBM.cpp, one
friend declaration in CDRMOutput, CDRMBackend and CDRMRenderer, and the vulkan dependency. The same patch applies
to v0.16.0 and to main.

Replaces the earlier four patches (0001-0003 CPU copy inside DRM.cpp/Renderer.cpp, 0004 GPU copy). New: one
damage journal for both engines, per-output fallback with a retry after a growing pause, counters in the trace,
and AQ_MGPU_GPU_COPY_VERIFY=<n> (compare samples of the scanout buffer with the rendered frame).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
